@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# Tester invites. Operators create invites in Harbor
# (tenantinvites.v1.TenantInviteAdminService); the invitee gets an email with
# APP_BASE_URL/signup?invite=<token>. Redeeming it creates a complimentary
# workspace: never billed, on the invite's tier and in its groups. Set
# inviteToken to the token from that link.
@inviteToken = paste-the-token-from-the-invite-link

### Signup mode — open | invite_only  [public, cacheable 30 s]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/signup-config

### Preview an invite — {email, expires_at}; every unusable token answers 410  [public, throttled]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tenant-invites/{{inviteToken}}

### Signup with a tester invite (expects 201; the email must be the invited one)  [public]
# Without invite_token while signup is invite-only: 403 {code: invite_required}.
# Another address: 403 {code: invite_email_mismatch}. Spent/expired/revoked: 410.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant": { "name": "Acme Beta" },
  "user": {
    "name": "Jane Okafor",
    "email": "jane@acme.com",
    "password": "s3cur3P@ssw0rd"
  },
  "invite_token": "{{inviteToken}}"
}

### Complimentary workspace — the entitlements read reports complimentary: true
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me/entitlements

### Switch tier for free (complimentary, no live subscription): 200 with the entitlements body, never a checkout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspace/plan
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tier_id": "pro" }

### Another workspace while invite-only — past the cap: 403 {code: workspace_limit}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Second workspace" }
